From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:59:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 96/98] Acceleration gates face their pocket the right way
 round

The client lines a gate model's z axis up with minus dunDirection, so
sending the line towards the next room left every gate facing away from
it (seen on the incursion gates). The direction is now reversed. This
covers mission and complex gates as well, which use the same code.
---
 src/eve-server/system/cosmicMgrs/DungeonMgr.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/eve-server/system/cosmicMgrs/DungeonMgr.cpp b/src/eve-server/system/cosmicMgrs/DungeonMgr.cpp
index 4a97909e..bef561ba 100644
--- a/src/eve-server/system/cosmicMgrs/DungeonMgr.cpp
+++ b/src/eve-server/system/cosmicMgrs/DungeonMgr.cpp
@@ -2399,6 +2399,9 @@ void DungeonMgr::MakeGateSlim(uint32 gateItemID, PyDict* slim)
             }
         }
     }
+    /* the client lines the gate model's z axis up with minus dunDirection (SpaceObject.AlignToDirection), which left the
+     *  gates facing away from their pocket in game, so it gets the reverse of the line to the room */
+    dir = GVector(-dir.x, -dir.y, -dir.z);
     PyList* dirList = new PyList();
         dirList->AddItem(new PyFloat(dir.x));
         dirList->AddItem(new PyFloat(dir.y));
